['Here's a simplified version of how such a function could be implemented in C++. Note that this code needs to be integrated into an existing system with proper error handling and logging mechanisms. This is just a basic outline of how the function might look like. Also, this code does not consider multi-threading and optimizations which are not covered here due to simplicity:

```cpp
#include <forward_list>
#include <string>
#include <cstdarg>
#include <cstdio>

// Function for logging with variadic arguments using snprintf
void log(const char* format, ...) {
    va_list args;
    va_start(args, format);
    vfprintf(stderr, format, args);
    fputs("\n", stderr);
    va_end(args);
}

// Function for logging or inserting after the target log entry
void logOrInsertAfter(std::forward_list<std::string>& logs, const std::string& targetLogEntry, const char* format, ...) {
    va_list args;
    va_start(args, format);

    // Format the log message using snprintf and va_args
    char buffer[512];  // Adjust size as needed
    vsnprintf(buffer, sizeof(buffer), format, args);

    auto it = logs.begin();
    bool foundTargetLogEntry = false;

    while (it != logs.end()) {
        if (*it == targetLogEntry) {
            foundTargetLogEntry = true;
            ++it;  // Move to the next entry for insertion
            break;
        }
        ++it;  // Move to the next log entry
    }

    if (foundTargetLogEntry) {
        logs.insert_after(it, buffer);
    } else {
        logs.push_front(buffer);  // Insert at end of list
    }

    va_end(args);
}
```

This code doesn't handle thread safety and potential memory leaks or other issues that might occur in a real-world distributed logging system. The design also assumes the forward_list is thread safe, which may not be the case for all STL containers. 

Also note, it uses `std::forward_list` as an example. For large-scale systems with millions of logs, a custom data structure might need to be used that takes advantage of low memory allocations and ensures good cache locality.
']

