["Here's a simple example implementation of RandomValueGenerator library with basic requirements for each point in your list:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Threading;

namespace RandomValueGeneratorLibrary
{
    public class RandomValueGenerator
    {
        private readonly ThreadLocal<Random> _random = new ThreadLocal<Random>(() => new Random());

        // Generate random float within specified range
        public float NextFloat(float minValue, float maxValue) 
        {
            if (minValue > maxValue) throw new ArgumentOutOfRangeException();

            return (float)(_random.Value.NextDouble() * (maxValue - minValue) + minValue);
        }

        // Generate random integer within specified range
        public int NextInt(int minValue, int maxValue) 
        {
            if (minValue > maxValue) throw new ArgumentOutOfRangeException();

            return _random.Value.Next(minValue, maxValue);
        }
    }
}
```
This library uses a ThreadLocal<Random> for each thread to ensure thread safety and optimal performance under high load conditions. 
For the configuration mechanism you could add properties in your class that can be adjusted dynamically by other parts of your system. For example:

