['This is a large task that requires substantial coding and architectural planning. Below I'll outline an approach using several Java libraries:

1) Apache HttpClient for making HTTP requests
2) Log4j/SLF4J for logging
3) Hystrix for the circuit breaker pattern
4) Apache Commons IO for file operations
5) Spring Cloud Sleuth and Zipkin for distributed tracing system.

```java
public class HighThroughputApplication {
    private static final Logger logger = LogManager.getLogger(HighThroughputApplication.class);
    private HystrixCommandProperties hystrixCommandProperties;
    private FileManagementApi fileManagementApi;

    public HighThroughputApplication() {
        // set up the properties for the Hystrix command
        this.hystrixCommandProperties = HystrixCommandProperties.Setter()
                .withExecutionTimeoutInMilliseconds(1000)
                .withCircuitBreakerRequestVolumeThreshold(5)
                .build();

        // instantiate the API client
        this.fileManagementApi = new FileManagementApi("https://api-endpoint/", "username", "password");
    }

    public void deleteFile(String filePath, int retryCount) {
        HystrixCommand<Void> command = new HystrixCommand.Setter()
                .withProperties(this.hystrixCommandProperties)
                .andCommandKey("delete-file")
                .andThreadPoolKey("delete-file-threads")
                .build();

        // wrap the operation in a command that will handle retries and circuit breaking
        HystrixCommand<Void> deleteFileCommand = new DeleteFileCommand(this.fileManagementApi, filePath, retryCount);

        try {
            deleteFileCommand.execute();
        } catch (Exception e) {
            logger.error("Failed to delete file: " + filePath, e);
        }
    }

    private class DeleteFileCommand extends HystrixCommand<Void> {
        private final FileManagementApi api;
        private final String filePath;
        private int retryCount;

        public DeleteFileCommand(FileManagementApi api, String filePath, int retryCount) {
            super(Setter.withGroupKey(HystrixCommandGroupKey.Factory.asKey("DeleteFileGroup")));
            this.api = api;
            this.filePath = filePath;
            this.retryCount = retryCount;
        }

        @Override
        protected Void run() throws Exception {
            try {
                // call the API to delete the file
                api.deleteFile(filePath);

                // log a success
                logger.info("Successfully deleted file: " + filePath);

                return null;
            } catch (Exception e) {
                if (retryCount > 0) {
                    // wait for an exponential backoff before retrying
                    int delay = (int) Math.pow(2, 5 - retryCount);

                    Thread.sleep(delay * 1000);

                    // try again with one less retry
                    deleteFile(filePath, retryCount - 1);
                } else {
                    throw e;
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```
Please note that this is just a basic example and doesn't take into account many aspects of your requirements like concurrent processing up to 10,000 operations per second or dynamic concurrency adjustment. Also, this code snippet does not handle network latency, packet loss or system health metrics in any meaningful way. The actual implementation would require more complex solutions including error handling, logging integration with existing infrastructure, and strategies for load balancing among others.
']

