The RetryStrategy class would look something like this:

```javascript
class RetryStrategy {
  constructor(func, context) {
    this.apiRequest = func.bind(context);
    this.retries = 0;
  }

  executeWithRetry(requestFunc, retryLimit=5) {
    return requestFunc()
      .catch(error => {
        if (this.retries < retryLimit) {
          this.retries++;
          return this.executeWithRetry(requestFunc);
        } else {
          throw error;
        }
      });
  }
}
```
