['This task requires a deep understanding of low-level programming concepts, such as memory management, multi-threading, network programming, error handling, configuration settings, logging, testing, and robust design patterns. Below is a basic implementation outline using the POSIX Threads (pthread) library for threading, libcurl for network communication, and sqlite3 for database operations. Note that this example does not include all your requirements as doing so would result in a massive codebase and might take days to write and test. 

```C
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <pthread.h>
#include <curl/curl.h>
#include <sqlite3.h>

typedef struct {
    int id;
    char* data;
} DataObject;

void *processData(void *arg) {
    DataObject *object = (DataObject *) arg;

    CURL *curl = curl_easy_init();
    if(!curl) {
        fprintf(stderr, "Failed to initialize libcurl\n");
        return NULL; 
    }

    // Perform API call using libcurl. Handle network issues and API errors.

    curl_easy_cleanup(curl);

    sqlite3 *db;
    if (sqlite3_open("test.db", &db) != SQLITE_OK) {
        fprintf(stderr, "Failed to open database\n");
        return NULL; 
    }

    // Write object data to the database using sqlite3 API. Handle errors.

    sqlite3_close(db);

    free(object->data);
    free(object);

    return NULL; 
}

int main() {
    pthread_t threads[10];

    for (int i = 0; i < 10; ++i) {
        DataObject *object = malloc(sizeof(DataObject));
        object->id = i;
        // Allocate and fill data, error checking omitted.

        pthread_create(&threads[i], NULL, processData, object);
    }

    for (int i = 0; i < 10; ++i) {
        pthread_join(threads[i], NULL);
    }

    return 0;
}
```
The above program creates a fixed number of threads that process and clean up data objects. It leverages libcurl for network communication, sqlite3 as a simple embedded database and pthread library for threading. Error handling was omitted in this simplified version but should be added according to your requirements. 

Please note that you'd need to install the necessary development libraries for libcurl (`libcurl4-openssl-dev`) and sqlite3 (`libsqlite3-dev`). You can compile it with `gcc -o program program.c -lpthread -lcurl -lsqlite3`.
']

