['The task you've described is quite complex and involves many sub-tasks. While I can provide a basic structure or pseudo code for the Union-Find algorithm, other aspects like integration with multiple external data sources, predictive analytics etc., are beyond the scope of this platform because they involve various libraries, protocols, cloud services, machine learning models, which are not typically used in simple text-based interfaces.

Here is a basic implementation of a union-find algorithm in Java:

```java
public class UnionFind {
    private int[] parent;
    private byte[] rank;
    private int count;

    public UnionFind(int n) {
        if (n < 0) throw new IllegalArgumentException();
        count = n;
        parent = new int[n];
        rank = new byte[n];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            parent[i] = i;
            rank[i] = 0;
        }
    }

    public int find(int p) {
        validate(p);
        while (p != parent[p]) {
            parent[p] = parent[parent[p]]; // path compression by halving
            p = parent[p];
        }
        return p;
    }

    public void union(int p, int q) {
        int rootP = find(p);
        int rootQ = find(q);
        if (rootP == rootQ) return;
        // make root of smaller rank point to root of larger rank
        if   (rank[rootP] < rank[rootQ]) parent[rootP] = rootQ;
        else {
            parent[rootQ] = rootP;
            if (rank[rootP] == rank[rootQ]) rank[rootP]++;
        }
        count--;
    }

    // validate that p is a valid index
    private void validate(int p) {
        int n = parent.length;
        if (p < 0 || p >= n) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("index " + p + " is not between 0 and " + (n-1));  
        }
    }
}
```
Please note that this Union-Find algorithm is for simplicity's sake, a real-world implementation would need to handle large data sets. This can be achieved by using distributed or parallel computing frameworks like Hadoop or Spark, or by using memory-mapped files (like MemoryMappedFile from Apache Commons) if dealing with extremely large datasets.
