["This is a complex task which can't be implemented here as it requires an elaborate understanding of your actual system architecture and the existing codebase to provide a complete solution with details implementation. However, I will guide you through creating a basic Cache class that follows LRU/ARC eviction policy. You would need to integrate this into your microservices architecture as per your needs:

```cpp
#include <list>
#include <unordered_map>
#include <mutex>

template<typename K, typename V>
class Cache {
private:
    struct Item {
        V value;
        typename std::list<K>::iterator itr;
    };

    std::unordered_map<K, Item> items;
    std::list<K> lruList, arcList;
    size_t lruSizeMax, arcSizeMax;
    mutable std::mutex mtx;

public:
    Cache(size_t lruSizeMax = 10000, size_t arcSizeMax = 2000) : lruSizeMax(lruSizeMax), arcSizeMax(arcSizeMax) { }

    bool get(const K &key, V *val) const {
        std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mtx);

        auto itr = items.find(key);
        if (itr == items.end())
            return false;

        // Move item to MRU end of ARC list
        arcList.splice(arcList.end(), arcList, itr->second.itr);
        *val = itr->second.value;
        return true;
    }

    void put(const K &key, const V &value) {
        std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mtx);

        if (items.find(key) != items.end()) {
            // Item is already in cache - update value and move to MRU end of ARC list
            auto itr = items[key].itr;

            *itr = key;
            arcList.splice(arcList.end(), arcList, itr);
            items[key].value = value;
        } else {
            // New item - add to cache and MRU end of ARC list
            if (lruSizeMax > 0) {
                lruList.push_back(key);
                auto itr = --lruList.end();

                items[key] = Item{value, itr};
                arcList.splice(arcList.begin(), lruList, itr);
            } else {
                // ARC eviction - remove LRU item from ARC list and add new item to both lists
                if (items.size() >= lruSizeMax + arcSizeMax) {
                    items.erase(arcList.front());
                    arcList.pop_front();
                }

                items[key] = Item{value, --lruList.end()};
            }
        }
    }

    void clear() {
        std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mtx);

        lruList.clear();
        arcList.clear();
        items.clear();
    }
};
```

This is a basic LRU/ARC Cache implementation and does not support GET and POST requests directly. It also requires an HTTP client for sending the actual GET and POST requests. Please note that there are many optimizations and other considerations that need to be addressed in your production codebase. This is a simplified example just for educational purposes.
"]

