["Your request involves creating a highly complex system that requires extensive knowledge of distributed systems, security protocols, error handling, and more. As such, it's beyond the capacity of this platform to provide a complete solution in a single response. 

However, I can give you an idea about how to structure your application using Express (a popular Node.js web application framework) as a backend. This will help you get started with some parts of your requirements like JWT validation, session management and admin controls:

```javascript
const express = require('express');
const jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');
const redis = require('redis');

// Initialize a Redis client for caching
const client = redis.createClient();

client.on('error', (err) => console.log(`Error ${err}`));

const app = express();
app.use(express.json()); // Parse incoming JSON data

// JWT Validation Middleware
function authenticateToken(req, res, next) {
  const authHeader = req.headers['authorization'];
  const token = authHeader && authHeader.split(' ')[1];

  if (token == null) return res.sendStatus(401); // If no token is provided

  jwt.verify(token, process.env.ACCESS_TOKEN_SECRET, (err, user) => {
    if (err) return res.sendStatus(403); // Invalid Token

    req.user = user;
    next();
  });
}

// Session Management Middleware
function manageSession(req, res, next) {
  const sessionId = req.headers['x-session-id'];

  if (sessionId == null) return res.sendStatus(401); // If no session ID is provided

  client.get(`sess:${sessionId}`, (err, data) => {
    if (!data || err) return res.sendStatus(403); // Invalid or expired session

    req.user = JSON.parse(data).user;
    next();
  });
}

// Admin Controls Middleware
function adminControls(req, res, next) {
  if (req.user.role !== 'admin') return res.sendStatus(403); // Only admins can perform this action

  next();
}
```
This is just a sample code and it does not cover the entire requirements of your system such as JWT token validation, session management, admin controls etc. You'll need to implement these features according to your specific needs.

For the other components like caching, error handling, data retention policies and so on, you will need to design and develop a separate module or service that interacts with these components as required by other parts of your system. This is just an example of how you could structure one part of this system using Node.js and Express, but building the entire system from scratch would be an enormous task.
