```java
import java.io.*;

public class CommandExecutor {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String command = "ls -l"; // replace this with your actual command
        File fileToDelete = new File("your_file"); // replace this with your file to delete if exists

        try {
            if (fileToDelete.exists() && !fileToDelete.delete()) {
                throw new IOException("Failed to delete the file " + fileToDelete);
            }

            Process process = Runtime.getRuntime().exec(command);

            BufferedReader outputReader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(process.getInputStream()));
            BufferedReader errorReader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(process.getErrorStream()));

            String line;
            while ((line = outputReader.readLine()) != null) {
                System.out.println(line);
            }

            if ((line = errorReader.readLine()) != null) {
                throw new IOException("Command execution failed with message: " + line);
            }
        } catch (IOException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }
}
```

This program first deletes a specified file if it exists, then executes the command passed as an argument and finally reads both output and error streams from the executed process. If any exception occurs during these operations, it is caught and its message is printed to the standard error stream. 

Remember, the actual implementation of such system requires much more than just this code snippet: from designing the overall architecture, implementing synchronization primitives for concurrent processing, managing network connections efficiently, dealing with third-party payment gateway APIs, etc. This solution should be used as a starting point and further enhancements are necessary to fully satisfy all constraints mentioned in your problem statement.
