["Here is the high level overview of how you can implement this task:

```java
import java.util.*;
import java.util.concurrent.*;

public class TopNIntegersService {
    private static final int N = 10000; // initial top N
    private ConcurrentMap<Integer, Integer> map = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();

    private PriorityQueue<Integer> queue = new PriorityQueue<>((a, b) -> map.get(b) - map.get(a));
    private Semaphore semaphore = new Semaphore(N);

    public void processDataStream() {
        while (true) { // continuously stream data
            int[] dataBatch = getNextBatchOfIntegers(); 

            ExecutorService executorService = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(dataBatch.length);
            for (int i = 0; i < dataBatch.length; i++) {
                Integer finalI = i;
                Future<?> future = executorService.submit(() -> {
                    semaphore.acquireUninterruptibly(); // thread pool manages concurrent access to queue and map

                    if (map.containsKey(dataBatch[finalI])) {
                        int count = map.get(dataBatch[finalI]);
                        queue.remove(dataBatch[finalI]); 
                        map.put(dataBatch[finalI], ++count); 
                        queue.offer(dataBatch[finalI]); 
                    } else {
                        map.put(dataBatch[finalI], 1);
                        queue.offer(dataBatch[finalI]);
                    }

                    if (queue.size() > N) { // remove least frequent integer
                        Integer num = queue.poll();
                        map.remove(num);
                    }
                    semaphore.release();
                });

                try {
                    future.get(); // wait for all tasks to finish
                } catch (InterruptedException | ExecutionException e) {
                    Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
                    return;
                } finally {
                    executorService.shutdownNow(); 
                }
            }
        }
    }

    private int[] getNextBatchOfIntegers() {
        // This is a placeholder for actual data stream, replace it with real implementation
        Random random = new Random();
        return random.ints(1000).toArray(); 
    }
}
```
This simple code snippet outlines the basic structure and logic of this task. It uses `ConcurrentHashMap` to track count of each integer, `PriorityQueue` to manage top N integers, and `Semaphore` for managing concurrency during multithreading environment. However, please note that it's a very simplified version and it doesn't cover all the requirements mentioned in your problem description. It needs further refactoring and enhancements to address complexities like network latency, backpressure management, error handling strategies etc. Also, this is just a starting point and there are many more considerations needed for designing such a system.
"]

