["This is a very comprehensive request and would be beyond the scope of this platform to provide a full-fledged code base that meets all these specifications. However, I can give you an example of how one might start developing some of these features using JavaScript. Here's a simple implementation for each feature:

1. Asynchronous DOM processing with concurrency control:
```javascript
class DomProcessor {
  constructor(domTree) {
    this.domTree = domTree;
    this.queue = [];
    this.activeTasks = 0;
    this.maxConcurrentTasks = 5; // adjust based on real-world constraints
  }

  processNode(node) {
    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
      // process the node here...
      resolve();
    });
  }

  addToQueue(node) {
    this.queue.push(() => this.processNode(node));
    this.dequeue();
  }

  dequeue() {
    while (this.activeTasks < this.maxConcurrentTasks && this.queue.length) {
      const task = this.queue.shift();
      this.activeTasks++;
      task().then(() => {
        this.activeTasks--;
        this.dequeue();
      });
    }
  }
}
```
2. Backoff and retry logic for third-party API:
```javascript
class ApiClient {
  constructor(baseUrl) {
    this.baseUrl = baseUrl;
    this.backoffDelay = 1000; // initial backoff delay in ms
  }

  async getData() {
    let result;
    while (!result) {
      try {
        const response = await fetch(this.baseUrl);
        if (response.ok) {
          result = await response.json();
        } else {
          throw new Error('API request failed');
        }
      } catch (error) {
        console.warn('Failed to get data from API, retrying...', error);
        // Backoff and retry
        await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, this.backoffDelay));
        this.backoffDelay *= 2; // double the backoff delay for every retry
      }
    }
    return result;
  }
}
```

Please note that creating a library as complex and comprehensive as you've described would require a detailed design process, careful implementation, rigorous testing, and ongoing maintenance. It also needs to be integrated with other systems like Kubernetes, orchestration tools, cloud services like AWS Lambda, and compliance requirements like GDPR and CCPA.
