["This task involves implementing several features of a large software project in Java, which includes data processing, memory management, security, error handling, multi-threading, distributed system design, monitoring, load balancing, self-healing, user interface and documentation. This is quite an extensive task that may not fit into a single code block. However, here's a simplified version of how you could structure some basic building blocks:

```java
import java.util.*;

public class UnionFindService {
    private Map<Integer, Integer> parent;
    private Map<Integer, Integer> rank;

    public UnionFindService() {
        this.parent = new HashMap<>();
        this.rank = new HashMap<>();
    }

    public void makeSet(int[] universe) {
        for (int i : universe)
            addElement(i);
    }

    public Integer find(int k) {
        if (parent.get(k) != k)
            parent.put(k, find(parent.get(k)));

        return parent.get(k);
    }

    public void union(int a, int b) {
        int x = find(a);
        int y = find(b);

        if (x == y)
            return;

        if (rank.get(x) > rank.get(y))
            parent.put(y, x);
        else if (rank.get(y) > rank.get(x))
            parent.put(x, y);
        else {
            parent.put(x, y);
            rank.put(y, rank.get(y) + 1);
        }
    }

    public void addElement(int k) {
        if (!parent.containsKey(k)) {
            parent.put(k, k);
            rank.put(k, 0);
        }
    }
}
```
Please note that this is a simplified version of the Union-Find algorithm and it doesn't cover all aspects you mentioned like dynamic memory allocation, failure handling, external data source integration, real-time feedback, predictive analytics, authentication and encryption, distributed lock mechanism, multi-node communication, self-healing mechanisms, user interface, documentation etc. You would need to further refine this codebase for production use.

