['This is quite a complex task and requires significant effort to implement as well as comprehensive knowledge about PHP programming, microservices architecture, configuration management systems, logging mechanisms, error tracking, security standards etc. 

I'll provide a simple example of how you might get started with setting up a configuration management system using PHP. It covers the basics like loading configurations from local files and environment variables. Please note that this is a simplification and doesn't cover all points mentioned in your task. For an actual implementation, you would need to implement more complex features like seamless switching between environments, integration with external APIs, error handling etc., which would likely require a larger codebase than can be provided here.

```php
class ConfigManager {
    private $config;

    public function __construct() {
        $this->loadConfig();
    }

    private function loadConfig() {
        // Load from local files
        $localFiles = ['.env', 'config.json'];

        foreach($localFiles as $file) {
            $path = __DIR__ . '/' . $file;
            if (file_exists($path)) {
                $this->loadFromFile($path);
            }
        }

        // Load from environment variables
        $envVars = ['DB_HOST', 'DB_USER'];

        foreach($envVars as $var) {
            $value = $this->getEnvVar($var);

            if ($value !== false) {
                $this->setConfigValue($var, $value);
            }
        }
    }

    private function loadFromFile($path) {
        $ext = pathinfo($path, PATHINFO_EXTENSION);

        if ($ext == 'env') {
            $this->loadDotEnvFile($path);
        } elseif ($ext == 'json') {
            $this->config = array_merge($this->config, $this->parseJsonFile($path));
        }
    }

    private function loadDotEnvFile($path) {
        $lines = file($path, FILE_IGNORE_NEW_LINES | FILE_SKIP_EMPTY_LINES);

        foreach ($lines as $line) {
            if (strpos(trim($line), '#') === 0) continue;

            list($name, $value) = explode('=', $line, 2);
            $this->setConfigValue(trim($name), trim($value));
        }
    }

    private function parseJsonFile($path) {
        $jsonString = file_get_contents($path);

        return json_decode($jsonString, true);
    }

    public function getConfigValue($name) {
        if (isset($this->config[$name])) {
            return $this->config[$name];
        } else {
            throw new Exception("Configuration value not found: " . $name);
        }
    }

    private function setConfigValue($name, $value) {
        $this->config[$name] = $value;
    }
}
```
This class loads configurations from local files (`.env` and `json`) and environment variables. It provides a simple interface to get the values of specific configuration settings. Note that this code doesn't include error handling or security measures, which you should add in your actual implementation.
']

