['Sure, here is an example of how you could implement the functionality to decrypt an encrypted message in C# using triple DES encryption. 

```CSharp
using System;
using System.Text;
using System.Security.Cryptography;

public class TripleDESCryptoHelper
{
    private readonly byte[] _key;
    private readonly byte[] _iv;

    public TripleDESCryptoHelper(string key, string iv)
    {
        _key = Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(key);
        _iv = Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(iv);

        Array.Resize(ref _key, 24); // Triple DES requires a 192-bit key size
    }

    public string DecryptFromBase64String(string encryptedText)
    {
        using (TripleDES tripleDes = TripleDES.Create())
        {
            tripleDes.Key = _key;
            tripleDes.IV = _iv;

            ICryptoTransform decryptor = tripleDes.CreateDecryptor(_key, _iv);
            byte[] encryptedBytes = Convert.FromBase64String(encryptedText);

            byte[] decryptedBytes = decryptor.TransformFinalBlock(encryptedBytes, 0, encryptedBytes.Length);
            return Encoding.UTF8.GetString(decryptedBytes);
        }
    }
}
```
This class takes a key and IV (Initialization Vector) as strings, converts them to bytes using UTF-8 encoding and stores them for use during decryption. The DecryptFromBase64String method takes an encrypted text string encoded in Base64, creates a TripleDES decryptor, decodes the Base64 string into bytes, applies the decryptor to get the original message and then converts it back to a UTF-8 string.

Please make sure that you have the required permissions for key usage on the machine where this code will be run. This can often require running as an administrator or granting explicit permissions. Also, make sure to use secure keys and IVs in your production application, as anyone with these could decrypt your data. 

Remember to add the necessary using directives at the top of your file: `using System;` , `using System.Text;` , `using System.Security.Cryptography;` .
']

