['Here's a basic outline for your `ServiceManager` microservice. It will not be fully functional as it requires a lot more code and configuration than just this snippet. Also, creating a production-ready service that can handle all those requirements is beyond the scope of this response. 

```java
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.*;
import java.util.UUID;

@RestController
public class ServiceManager {
    private final ServiceStateService serviceStateService;
    private final ExternalSystemIntegration externalSystemIntegration;
    private final SecurityService securityService;

    public ServiceManager(ServiceStateService serviceStateService, 
                          ExternalSystemIntegration externalSystemIntegration, 
                          SecurityService securityService) {
        this.serviceStateService = serviceStateService;
        this.externalSystemIntegration = externalSystemIntegration;
        this.securityService = securityService;
    }

    @PostMapping("/start")
    public void start(@RequestBody StartRequest request, @RequestHeader("Authorization") String token) {
        UUID userId = securityService.getUserIdFromToken(token);
        DynamicDelay dynamicDelay = serviceStateService.getDynamicDelay(request.getServiceName());

        if (serviceStateService.isRunning(request.getServiceName())) {
            return;
        } 

        // Start the service after delay
        try {
            Thread.sleep(dynamicDelay.getDelayInMilliseconds());
            externalSystemIntegration.startService(request.getServiceName(), userId);
        } catch (InterruptedException e) {
            Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
        }
    }

    @PostMapping("/stop")
    public void stop(@RequestBody StopRequest request, @RequestHeader("Authorization") String token) {
        UUID userId = securityService.getUserIdFromToken(token);

        if (!serviceStateService.isRunning(request.getServiceName())) {
            return;
        } 

        // Stop the service
        externalSystemIntegration.stopService(request.getServiceName(), userId);
    }

    @GetMapping("/status/{serviceName}")
    public String status(@PathVariable String serviceName) {
        return serviceStateService.isRunning(serviceName) ? "RUNNING" : "STOPPED";
    }
}
```

For the full implementation, it would be better to use a framework like Spring Boot and follow good practices of microservices architecture, such as using Eureka for service discovery, Ribbon for client-side load balancing, Hystrix for fault tolerance and circuit breakers. 

