['Below is an example of how you can implement the RandomValueGenerator class in C#. 

```Csharp
using System;

public class RandomValueGenerator : ILogger
{
    private float minValue;
    private float maxValue;

    public RandomValueGenerator(float min, float max)
    {
        if (min > max) throw new ArgumentException("Minimum value can't be greater than maximum value");

        this.minValue = min;
        this.maxValue = max;
    }

    public float GenerateRandomFloat()
    {
        Random random = new Random();
        double val = (random.NextDouble() * (this.maxValue - this.minValue) + this.minValue);
        return (float)val;
    }

    public int GenerateRandomInteger()
    {
        Random random = new Random();
        return random.Next((int)Math.Ceiling(this.minValue), (int)Math.Floor(this.maxValue));
    }

    public override string ToString()
    {
        return $"Current Range: [{this.minValue}, {this.maxValue}]";
    }

    public void LogError(Exception ex, string message)
    {
        // Implement a method for logging errors here
    }
}
```

This code includes the class `RandomValueGenerator` that generates random floating-point and integer values within a specified range. It uses two private fields, minValue and maxValue, to store these ranges. The constructor takes in the minimum and maximum value as parameters and initializes them. If the minValue is greater than maxValue, it throws an exception.

The `GenerateRandomFloat` method generates a random float between minValue and maxValue using Random().NextDouble() function. 

The `GenerateRandomInteger` method generates a random integer between minValue and maxValue using Random().Next() function.

It also overrides the `ToString` method to display the current range settings.

