    pthread_t tid[N];
    srand((unsigned int)time(NULL));

    for (int i=0; i<N; ++i){
        if(pthread_create(&tid[i], NULL, &addToList, NULL)){
            printf("Failed to create thread\n"); 
            return -1; 
        }
         usleep(500); // To avoid creating all threads at once and reducing latency. Remove this for production code.
    }

    for (int i=0; i<N; ++i){
       pthread_join(tid[i], NULL); 
    }

    return 0;
}
```
Please note that the above code is a simple demonstration of how you might use threads to add items to a linked list. It doesn't implement the real-time data fetching and validation against pre-defined reference table, error handling mechanisms, or logging. Implementing these features requires an in-depth understanding of your specific requirements and the external API used for real-time data fetching and validation.
